// Logbook's conceptual schema, as the verbalizer says it: docs/CSDP.md,
// steps 2 to 7, a statement a line. Logbook.orm is built from it:
//
//   ormtool build Model/Logbook.forml Model/Logbook.orm
//
// Each "# heading" is a diagram. A line starting "*" (derived), "**"
// (derived and stored), "+" (partly derived) or "++" (partly, and stored)
// is the rule of the fact type on the line before.

# People and vehicles

User is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .email
PersonName is a value type.
Portable data type: Text: Variable Length
Vehicle is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .id
Portable data type: Other: Object ID
VehicleName is a value type.
Portable data type: Text: Variable Length
Make is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .name
CarModel is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .name
Fuel is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .name
Year is a value type.
Portable data type: Numeric: Unsigned Small Integer
VIN is a value type.
Portable data type: Text: Fixed Length(17)
RegistrationNumber is a value type.
Portable data type: Text: Variable Length
Date is a value type.
Portable data type: Temporal: Date
Duration is a value type.
Portable data type: Numeric: Unsigned Small Integer

Vehicle (as OwnedVehicle) is owned by User (as Owner)
Each Vehicle is owned by exactly one User.
VehicleDriver is where User drives Vehicle.
++ The vehicle's owner drives it; the users it is shared with are entered.
User has PersonName
Each User has at most one PersonName.
Vehicle has VehicleName
Each Vehicle has exactly one VehicleName.
Vehicle is of Make
Each Vehicle is of exactly one Make.
Vehicle is of CarModel
Each Vehicle is of exactly one CarModel.
Vehicle was built in Year (as ManufactureYear)
Each Vehicle was built in exactly one Year.
Vehicle uses Fuel
Each Vehicle uses exactly one Fuel.
Vehicle has VIN
Each Vehicle has at most one VIN.
// Seventeen letters and digits, no I, O or Q.
The possible values of VIN match the pattern '[A-HJ-NPR-Z0-9]{17}'.
Vehicle has RegistrationNumber
Each Vehicle has at most one RegistrationNumber.

The possible values of Year are at least 1886.
The possible values of Duration are at least 1.

# Money and units

Amount is a value type.
Portable data type: Numeric: Decimal(19, 4)
Currency is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .code
Portable data type: Text: Fixed Length(3)
Quantity is a value type.
Portable data type: Numeric: Decimal(15, 3)
DistanceUnit is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .code
VolumeUnit is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .code
Factor is a value type.
Portable data type: Numeric: Decimal(19, 8)

Money has Amount
Each Money has exactly one Amount.
Money is in Currency
Each Money is in exactly one Currency.
For each Amount and Currency, at most one Money has that Amount and is in that Currency.
This association with Amount and Currency provides the preferred identification scheme for Money.

Distance has Quantity
Each Distance has exactly one Quantity.
Distance is in DistanceUnit
Each Distance is in exactly one DistanceUnit.
For each Quantity and DistanceUnit, at most one Distance has that Quantity and is in that DistanceUnit.
This association with Quantity and DistanceUnit provides the preferred identification scheme for Distance.

Volume has Quantity
Each Volume has exactly one Quantity.
Volume is in VolumeUnit
Each Volume is in exactly one VolumeUnit.
For each Quantity and VolumeUnit, at most one Volume has that Quantity and is in that VolumeUnit.
This association with Quantity and VolumeUnit provides the preferred identification scheme for Volume.

Currency (as BaseCurrency) was worth Factor in Currency (as QuoteCurrency) on Date
Fact Type Name: ExchangeRate
++ If on a date one X is worth F Y, then one Y is worth 1 / F X; a rate entered by hand both ways keeps the one entered.
For each Currency1, Currency2 and Date, that Currency1 was worth at most one Factor in that Currency2 on that Date.

User prefers Currency
Each User prefers at most one Currency.
User measures distance in DistanceUnit
Each User measures distance in at most one DistanceUnit.
User measures volume in VolumeUnit
Each User measures volume in at most one VolumeUnit.

The possible values of Amount are above 0.
The possible values of Quantity are at least 0.
The possible values of Factor are above 0.
The possible values of DistanceUnit are 'km', 'mi'.
The possible values of VolumeUnit are 'L', 'gal (US)', 'gal (imp)'.
// A currency code is ISO 4217's: three capital letters.
The possible values of Currency match the pattern '[A-Z]{3}'.

# What a vehicle cost, and is worth

Vehicle was acquired on Date (as PurchaseDate)
Each Vehicle was acquired on at most one Date.
Vehicle was acquired at Distance (as PurchaseMileage)
Each Vehicle was acquired at at most one Distance.
Vehicle was acquired for Money (as PurchasePrice)
Each Vehicle was acquired for at most one Money.
Vehicle is expected to be kept for Duration (as KeepDuration)
Each Vehicle is expected to be kept for at most one Duration.
Vehicle is expected to be driven Distance (as KeepDistance) more
Each Vehicle is expected to be driven at most one Distance more.
Vehicle is expected to sell for Money (as ExpectedSalePrice)
Each Vehicle is expected to sell for at most one Money.
Vehicle was valued on Date at Money (as Valuation)
For each Vehicle and Date, that Vehicle was valued on that Date at at most one Money.
Vehicle was sold on Date (as SaleDate)
* The date of the moment of the vehicle's CarSale.
Each Vehicle was sold on at most one Date.
Vehicle was sold for Money (as SellingPrice)
* What the vehicle's CarSale earned.
Each Vehicle was sold for at most one Money.
For each Vehicle, if that Vehicle was acquired on some Date1 and that Vehicle was sold on some Date2 then Date1 is less than or equal to Date2.

# Records

Moment is a value type.
Portable data type: Temporal: Date & Time
Note is a value type.
Portable data type: Text: Large Length
FileName is a value type.
Portable data type: Text: Variable Length
Record is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .id
Portable data type: Other: Object ID
Attachment is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .id
Portable data type: Other: Object ID
CostKind is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .name

Record is of Vehicle
++ A reminder from a schedule is of the schedule's vehicle.
Each Record is of exactly one Vehicle.
Record was entered by User (as EnteredBy) / User entered Record
Each Record was entered by exactly one User.
Record has Note
Each Record has at most one Note.
Attachment is of Record
Each Attachment is of exactly one Record.
Attachment has FileName
Each Attachment has exactly one FileName.

Each Event is a Record.
Event was at Moment (as Timestamp)
Each Event was at exactly one Moment.
Event had driver User (as Driver)
Each Event had driver exactly one User.
Each MeteredEvent is an Event.
MeteredEvent was at Distance (as Mileage)
Each MeteredEvent was at exactly one Distance.

Record cost Money (as Total)
++ A service's: the sum of its items' costs, less its discount, in its currency.
Each Record cost at most one Money.
Each Cost is by definition a Record that cost some Money.
Cost was charged Money (as Charged)
Each Cost was charged at most one Money.
Cost is of CostKind
* A fill-up is of 'Fuel', a tyre set of 'Tyres', a document of 'Documents'; a service or an expense of the kind it says.
Each Cost is of exactly one CostKind.

If some Event had driver some User and that Event is of some Vehicle then that User drives that Vehicle.
If some Record was entered by some User and that Record is of some Vehicle then that User drives that Vehicle.

// The meter goes up: a vehicle's later reading, in the same unit, ought
// not to be lower. Ought: the owner may enter history out of order.
Query MeterGoesUp:
It is forbidden that:
✓MeteredEvent1
  + was at Moment1
  + was at Distance1
    + has Quantity1
    + is in DistanceUnit1
  + is of Vehicle
    + Record is of that Vehicle
      + is Event
        + is MeteredEvent2
          + was at Moment2 > Moment1
          + was at Distance2
            + has Quantity2 < Quantity1
            + is in DistanceUnit1

# Meter readings and trips

Place is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .name
Purpose is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .name

Each MeterReading is a MeteredEvent.
Each Trip is a MeteredEvent.
Trip ended at Moment
Each Trip ended at exactly one Moment.
Trip ended at Distance
Each Trip ended at exactly one Distance.
Trip went from Place
Each Trip went from at most one Place.
Trip went to Place
Each Trip went to at most one Place.
Trip has Purpose
Each Trip has at most one Purpose.
For each Trip, if that Trip was at some Moment1 and that Trip ended at some Moment2 then Moment1 is less than or equal to Moment2.
// That a trip ends no nearer than it started compares distances, which
// are a quantity and a unit each: a rule, later.

# Fill-ups

Station is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .name

Each FillUp is a MeteredEvent.
Each FillUp is a Cost.
FillUp was of Volume
Each FillUp was of exactly one Volume.
FillUp was of Fuel
Each FillUp was of exactly one Fuel.
FillUp was at Station
Each FillUp was at exactly one Station.
FillUp filled the tank
It is obligatory that if some FillUp was of some Fuel and that FillUp is of some Vehicle then that Vehicle uses that Fuel.

# Services

Title is a value type.
Portable data type: Text: Variable Length
Instalments is a value type.
Portable data type: Numeric: Unsigned Small Integer
Garage is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .name
Task is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .name
PaymentMethod is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .name
ServiceItem is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .id
Portable data type: Other: Object ID

Each ServiceKind is by definition a CostKind that is 'Maintenance' or 'Repair'.
Each ExpenseKind is a CostKind.
Each Service is a MeteredEvent.
Each Service is a Cost.
Service has Title
Each Service has at most one Title.
Service was done by Garage
Each Service was done by exactly one Garage.
Service is of ServiceKind
Each Service is of exactly one ServiceKind.
Service is paid in Currency
Each Service is paid in exactly one Currency.
Service had a discount of Money
Each Service had a discount of at most one Money.
Service was paid by PaymentMethod
Each Service was paid by at most one PaymentMethod.
Service was paid in Instalments
Each Service was paid in at most one Instalments.

ServiceItem is part of Service
Each ServiceItem is part of exactly one Service.
ServiceItem is of Task
Each ServiceItem is of exactly one Task.
ServiceItem cost Money (as Cost)
Each ServiceItem cost exactly one Money.
ServiceItem was charged Money (as Charged)
Each ServiceItem was charged at most one Money.
ServiceItem has Note
Each ServiceItem has at most one Note.

The possible values of Instalments are at least 1.

# Tyres

TyreSetName is a value type.
Portable data type: Text: Variable Length
TyreSize is a value type.
Portable data type: Text: Variable Length
Tread is a value type.
Portable data type: Numeric: Decimal(4, 1)
Season is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .name
TyreModel is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .name

Each TyreSet is a Record.
TyreSet has TyreSetName
Each TyreSet has exactly one TyreSetName.
TyreSet is for Season
Each TyreSet is for exactly one Season.
TyreSet is of TyreModel
Each TyreSet is of exactly one TyreModel.
TyreSet is of TyreSize
Each TyreSet is of exactly one TyreSize.
TyreSet was bought on Date
Each TyreSet was bought on at most one Date.
For each TyreSet, that TyreSet was bought on some Date if and only if that TyreSet cost some Money.

Each TyreChange is a MeteredEvent.
TyreChange fitted TyreSet
Each TyreChange fitted exactly one TyreSet.
TyreChange removed TyreSet
* The set the vehicle's tyre change before it fitted; none for the first change recorded.
Each TyreChange removed at most one TyreSet.
TyreChange measured Tread
Each TyreChange measured exactly one Tread.
No TyreChange fitted and removed the same TyreSet.
If some TyreChange fitted some TyreSet and that TyreChange is of some Vehicle then that TyreSet is of that Vehicle.

The possible values of Season are 'Summer', 'Winter', 'All-season'.
The possible values of Tread are 0 to 20.

# Documents and expenses

Issuer is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .name
DocumentNumber is a value type.
Portable data type: Text: Variable Length
DocumentKind is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .name

Each Document is a Record.
Document is of DocumentKind
Each Document is of exactly one DocumentKind.
Document was issued by Issuer
Each Document was issued by exactly one Issuer.
Document has DocumentNumber
Each Document has exactly one DocumentNumber.
Document is valid from Date
Each Document is valid from exactly one Date.
Document expires on Date
Each Document expires on at most one Date.
For each Document, if that Document is valid from some Date1 and that Document expires on some Date2 then Date1 is less than Date2.

Each Expense is an Event.
Each Expense is a Cost.
Expense is of ExpenseKind
Each Expense is of exactly one ExpenseKind.

# Incomes

IncomeKind is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .name

Each Income is an Event.
Income is of IncomeKind
Each Income is of exactly one IncomeKind.
Income earned Money (as Earned)
Each Income earned exactly one Money.
Income was at Distance (as Mileage)
Each Income was at at most one Distance.
Income was paid in Instalments
Each Income was paid in at most one Instalments.
Income was for Trip
Each Income was for at most one Trip.
For each Trip, at most one Income was for that Trip.
If some Income was for some Trip and that Income is of some Vehicle then that Trip is of that Vehicle.
Each CarSale is by definition an Income that is of IncomeKind 'Car sale'.
// A vehicle is sold at most once: "Vehicle was sold on Date" is unique
// for the vehicle, and derived from its car sales.

# Checklists and inspections

ChecklistName is a value type.
Portable data type: Text: Variable Length
QuestionText is a value type.
Portable data type: Text: Variable Length
OptionText is a value type.
Portable data type: Text: Variable Length
Position is a value type.
Portable data type: Numeric: Unsigned Small Integer
Checklist is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .id
Portable data type: Other: Object ID
Question is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .id
Portable data type: Other: Object ID
Option is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .id
Portable data type: Other: Object ID
AnswerKind is an entity type.
Reference Mode: .name
YesNo is a value type.
Portable data type: Text: Variable Length

Checklist is kept by User
Each Checklist is kept by exactly one User.
Checklist has ChecklistName
Each Checklist has exactly one ChecklistName.
Question is in Checklist
Each Question is in exactly one Checklist.
Question says QuestionText
Each Question says exactly one QuestionText.
Question is at Position
Each Question is at exactly one Position.
For each Checklist and Position, at most one Question is in that Checklist and is at that Position.
Question is answered by AnswerKind
Each Question is answered by exactly one AnswerKind.
Option is in Question
Each Option is in exactly one Question.
Option says OptionText
Each Option says exactly one OptionText.
Option is at Position
Each Option is at exactly one Position.
For each Question and Position, at most one Option is in that Question and is at that Position.

Each Inspection is a MeteredEvent.
Inspection went through Checklist
Each Inspection went through exactly one Checklist.
If some Inspection went through some Checklist then some Question is in that Checklist.
If some Inspection went through some Checklist and that Inspection is of some Vehicle that is owned by some User then that Checklist is kept by that User.

Answer is where Inspection answered Question.
If some Inspection answered some Question then that Inspection went through some Checklist and that Question is in that Checklist.
Answer says YesNo
Each Answer says at most one YesNo.
Answer chose Option
In each population of Answer chose Option, each Answer, Option combination occurs at most once.
Answer has Note
Each Answer has at most one Note.
// An answer's options are of its question; a yes-or-no question's answers
// say yes or no and choose nothing; only an any-of question has options.
Query AnswerOptionsOfItsQuestion:
It is impossible that:
✓Answer
  + involves Question1
  + chose Option
    + is in Question2 <> Question1

Query YesOrNoAnswers:
It is impossible that:
✓Answer
  + says YesNo
  + involves Question
    + is answered by AnswerKind = 'Any of'

Query AnyOfAnswers:
It is impossible that:
✓Answer
  + chose Option
  + involves Question
    + is answered by AnswerKind = 'Yes or no'

Query OptionsOfAnyOfQuestions:
It is impossible that:
✓Question
  + is answered by AnswerKind = 'Yes or no'
  + Option is in that Question

The possible values of AnswerKind are 'Yes or no', 'Any of'.
The possible values of YesNo are 'Yes', 'No'.
The possible values of Position are at least 1.

# Schedules and reminders

Each Schedule is a Record.
Schedule is for Task
Each Schedule is for at most one Task.
Schedule is for ExpenseKind
Each Schedule is for at most one ExpenseKind.
Schedule is for Checklist
Each Schedule is for at most one Checklist.
For each Schedule, exactly one of the following holds: that Schedule is for some Task; that Schedule is for some ExpenseKind; that Schedule is for some Checklist.
Schedule recurs after Distance (as Interval)
Each Schedule recurs after at most one Distance.
Schedule recurs after Duration
Each Schedule recurs after at most one Duration.
Each Schedule recurs after some Distance or recurs after some Duration.

Each Reminder is a Record.
Reminder comes from Schedule
Each Reminder comes from at most one Schedule.
Reminder is for Task
Each Reminder is for at most one Task.
Reminder is for ExpenseKind
Each Reminder is for at most one ExpenseKind.
Reminder is for Checklist
Each Reminder is for at most one Checklist.
For each Reminder, exactly one of the following holds: that Reminder comes from some Schedule; that Reminder is for some Task; that Reminder is for some ExpenseKind; that Reminder is for some Checklist.
If some Reminder comes from some Schedule and that Reminder is of some Vehicle then that Schedule is of that Vehicle.
Reminder is due at Distance (as DueMileage)
++ A schedule's next reminder: the distance its last was done at, and the schedule's interval; the owner may change it.
Each Reminder is due at at most one Distance.
Reminder is due on Date (as DueDate)
++ A schedule's next reminder: the date its last was done on, and the schedule's interval; the owner may change it.
Each Reminder is due on at most one Date.
Each Reminder is due at some Distance or is due on some Date.
Reminder was done at Moment (as DoneAt)
++ The moment of the event that did its work, when one did.
Each Reminder was done at at most one Moment.
Reminder was done at Distance (as DoneMileage)
++ The distance of the event that did its work, when one did.
Each Reminder was done at at most one Distance.
For each Reminder, that Reminder was done at some Moment if and only if that Reminder was done at some Distance.
Reminder was done by Event
++ The first event of its vehicle, after it was set, that does its work: a service with an item of its task, an expense of its kind, an inspection through its checklist.
Each Reminder was done by at most one Event.
If some Reminder was done by some Event then that Reminder was done at some Moment.
If some Reminder was done by some Event and that Reminder is of some Vehicle then that Event is of that Vehicle.
// A schedule has at most one reminder not yet done.
Query OneOpenReminder:
It is impossible that:
✓Schedule
  + Reminder comes from that Schedule
    + not was done at Moment
    + count(Reminder) for Schedule > 1
